       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the maximum for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6 g/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Even with normal liver function, this dose risks hepatotoxicity. A 70 kg patient is also not in a weight-based exception.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that. Many systems will also need a pharmacist review for that dose."
